AGENTS.md:23:Most tests run the real on-device model on CPU. `tests/setup-shared-model.ts` loads it once per test file and shares it across services (`dispose()` is a no-op there), so tests that assert model-disposal behavior see the shared instance. On first run it downloads (~25 MB) into `~/.cache/desert-ant-models`. `vitest.config.ts` sets a 30 s timeout and `fileParallelism: false` on purpose, because parallel files each load a model and oversubscribe the CPU. Don't change those to speed things up.
AGENTS.md:43:**Experimental: masker-mini backend (`src/services/masker-mini/`)**: opt-in, for side-by-side trials only. `RedactorService` consumes the minimal `NerEngine` interface (`src/services/ner-engine.ts`). Env vars, read at load time in `getRedactInstance()`: `PI_PII_REDACT_BACKEND` = `desert-ant` (default) | `masker-mini`; `PI_PII_REDACT_MASKER_VARIANT` = `int4` (default) | `fp16`; `PI_PII_REDACT_MASKER_DIR` uses files from that directory (hashes still verified), otherwise files are downloaded from a pinned Hugging Face revision into `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/pi-pii-redact/masker-mini/<rev>/` (default `~/.cache`) and SHA-256 verified. It needs the dev dependencies `onnxruntime-node` and `@huggingface/tokenizers`, loaded lazily. Real-model tests run with `PI_PII_REDACT_TEST_MASKER=1`; `PI_PII_REDACT_BACKEND=masker-mini npm test` runs the whole suite against it.
AGENTS.md:46:- Redaction: `input`, `tool_result` (including `structuredContent`) and `context`. `context` re-redacts the whole history before every provider request.
